1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Welcome to the new feature introduction video of Marvelous Designer 2025.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Now you can convert the action files from other software or platform creation to the action files that match the default virtual model of Marvelous Designer.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Here I use the free files downloaded on Mixamo.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Search on the website and apply the action files you need.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Search for keywords in the search box, then double-click to apply the action on the website to the default model or the virtual model you uploaded.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Check all settings, such as arm space, etc.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Then click download, select the FBX file in the pop-up menu, and return to Marvelous Designer after downloading the desired option.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Go to the top of the main menu, and the virtual model is automatically converted into an action, then select gender in the window.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Here select the virtual model gender of the action.

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:14,000
After that, our action files can be stored and used for other virtual models, then open the downloaded FBX file and click convert.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Marvelous Designer will automatically convert the FBX file to a software-adjustable MTN action file.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
It is a very convenient and easy way to convert the FBX file into a software-adjustable MTN action file.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The FBX file is a very convenient and easy way to convert the FBX file into a software-adjustable MTN action file.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,000
When the conversion is completed, click the save button and select the save path.

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Name the unpreserved action file and place it in the right place.

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Then click on the bottom triangle at the bottom of the screen to open the animation editor.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
In the play area, click the mouse button on the right to select the range to be limited to the activity frame.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
This can set the starting and ending frames of the play area to the first and last frame with animation.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:09,000
In the play area, click the mouse button to put in the first frame.

20
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,000
You will see a list of all the action files in the play area that I have created previously.

21
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Go to the main menu and click on opening.

22
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Click on the top line of the window.

23
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Select the costume option and click OK.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Then, in the pop-up window, select the current virtual model size and posture option.

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
After wearing the costume, set the simulation quality to animation.

26
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:43,000
This setting will help you record more stable and accurate animation simulation data.

27
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Click the record button and start recording the costume animation as the character moves.

28
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
When the recording is complete, check if the costume animation is correctly recorded.

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Now you can easily use the external animation file.

30
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
The action file can also be used for a virtual model after joint printing.

31
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Please check the following tutorial.

